+# Design — From History to Signal
+
+## Frame
+
+- Canvas: 1920 × 1080
+- Safe padding: 120px, with all lesson content above the 960px content boundary
+- Background: deep navy with restrained paper panels; no gradients
+- Persistent furniture: program label at top left, module marker at top right, progress signal along the lower content edge
+
+## Type
+
+- Proxima Nova with the provided system fallback
+- Headings: 72–104px, weight 900
+- Supporting copy: 40–48px, weight 400 or 700
+- Labels: 22px, weight 700, uppercase, tracked
+
+## Storyboard
+
+1. A crowded archive obscures a small “NEXT” marker.
+2. The archive clears; a gold signal line switches on.
+3. Three scan targets appear: results, scope, alignment.
+4. Duty language creates friction while the future target remains out of focus.
+5. A task statement transforms into a measurable result.
+6. The lesson title resolves: history becomes signal.
+7. Move one selects forward-pointing evidence.
+8. Move two rebuilds bullets around results, scope, and impact.
+9. Move three turns a current-role profile toward future direction.
+10. A curator’s frame selects only evidence that supports the Next Move Statement.
+11. A line visibly connects NOW to BECOMING.
+12. The guiding question resolves to a confident “closer to yes.”
+
+## Motion
+
+One paused GSAP timeline controls the complete composition. Each timed clip receives a short entrance and exit. The progress signal advances beat by beat; the final beat adds a single resolve in its last second.
